==============================================================================
TOP 15 INTERVIEW QUESTIONS - SPLITERATOR & STREAM INTERNALS
==============================================================================

1. What is Spliterator?

Answer:
Spliterator stands for:

Split + Iterator

It is used internally by Streams to traverse and split data for parallel processing.

Flow:

Collection
    ↓
Spliterator
    ↓
Stream Pipeline

Interview One-Liner:
Spliterator is an iterator that can split data for parallel processing. 【1-1c4ebb】

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. Why was Spliterator introduced?

Answer:

Iterator
---------
Can traverse

Cannot split

Spliterator
------------
Can traverse
Can split

Benefits:

✓ Parallel Processing
✓ Better Performance
✓ Work Stealing Support

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. What does tryAdvance() do?

Answer:
Processes one element at a time.

Input:
[10,20,30]

Code:

spliterator.tryAdvance(
    System.out::println);

Output:
10

Call Again:

Output:
20

Call Again:

Output:
30

Interview Tip:
tryAdvance() moves one element forward.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. What does forEachRemaining() do?

Answer:
Processes all remaining elements.

Input:
[10,20,30]

Code:

spliterator.forEachRemaining(
    System.out::println);

Output:
10
20
30

Difference:

tryAdvance()
-------------
One at a time

forEachRemaining()
------------------
All remaining elements

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5. What does trySplit() do?

Answer:
Divides data into smaller chunks.

Input:
[1,2,3,4,5,6]

Code:

Spliterator<Integer> sp1 =
list.spliterator();

Spliterator<Integer> sp2 =
sp1.trySplit();

Possible Split:

sp1 → [4,5,6]

sp2 → [1,2,3]

Use:
Parallel Streams

Interview One-Liner:
trySplit() enables task splitting in parallel processing.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

